A||||8||Shaun41178||Raced a 4th Gen Camaro
Z||000000||Shaun41178||07-15-99||06:37 PM||||On my way to Windsor tonight to go to the casino(only won $15 but better then losing right?) So I top off the tank and I approach the onramp to the freeway(I-75). At the redlight is a white 4th gen camaro which I slowly pull in behind as I am in no hurry and also cause my freind and I are chatting. I notice that this camaro had dual custom chrome tips. So because I see dual tips I immediately think "Z". I turn off my radio so I could hear the exhaust note. The camaro pulls away and then gets on it up the onramp. Exhaust had a nice rumble to it. <br>So I am following along up the onramp behind and the camaro had to slow down as he quickly approached traffic of 60 and the guy took the onramp at about 70-75. The guy pulls in the slow lane behind a big rig and I go by about 5 miles an hour more and notice that his car has the word "Camaro" on the front qtr panel. So at this time I pretty much assume that it is a V6. Whether or not it was a 3800 or a 3.4 I don't know.<br>About 2 minutes after I pass the camaro he comes flying up my butt so I move into the slow lane so he can pass. At this point I am doing about 60-65. The camaro slows to my speed and gooses it. So I oblige and since he had a bumber on me I just punched it. I pull his bumber immediately and then he is on it. About a second later the camaro's bumper is at my door and I am slowly pulling and I mean slowly. We got up to 95 and I shut down as I had about 3/4 car length on him as his bumper was at my rear wheel and we were also approaching traffic. My friend was luaghing his ass off as soon as I hit the throttle. I guess he thought it was funny we were racing. The best part is is that he had his girl with him too! I bet he felt a little embarresed :O)<br>I slow down to give him a thumbs up but he is exiting and I try waving and have my freind wave but he doesn't look over but he gives it a rev so I am assuming he is saying good race?<br>Oh yea I forgot to mention that I did not have my nitrous on either. All engine baby. I was going on a hour or so long trip so I did not feel the need to be involved in a race or to even look for one. I guess one found me though. That was also the first time that I did not instigate a race with another car. This guy wanted to race me.<br>Ahhh another car loses to the almighty Fiero!!<br>------------------<br>2.8V6 3.08 FD 3 spd auto <br>Crane HI6S ignition <br>PS-91 Coil<br>Accel 8.8 mm wires<br>Throttle Body bypass<br>Ported exhaust manifolds<br>NOS 70 hp shot<br>Future mods: Hi lift cam full port and polish of heads and intake, <br>shift kit, underdrive pulley, custom intake with K&N cone, 2.25 cat-back with flowmaster muffler<br>Currently 200 hp @ wheels before ported exhaust manifolds<br>Best e.t. to date: 14.8@91 60' 2.07 <br>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178
Z||000001||PaUL||07-15-99||07:49 PM||||hey Shaun,<br>So you installed that muffler I sent you? How is sound and did it improve the power any?
Z||000002||Cooter||07-15-99||10:25 PM||||Shaun- Cool story! I finally won a race in my mighty 4 cyl Fiero. The guy had me through 2nd gear but when I hit 3rd, I started to pull away. But then he had to stop at another mail box. Damn those mail jeeps!  LOL
Z||000003||Shaun41178||07-16-99||01:13 AM||||Actually paul I have not installed the muffler yet.  You would have thought by now right?  I went and got a quote from a muffler shop and they said they could bend me a 2.5 inch system and install everything for about $135.  Plus do a little work on the cat if you catch my drift.  A great deal if you ask me.  $135 for the install and $50 for the muffler comes to less then $200.  I am expecting a 5-10 hp jump but mostly in the upper rpm range.  I am waiting for other mods to get done before I have the exhaust installed.  The most expensive part of the whole new exhaust will be the tips.  I am going to go with Borlas and have yet to decide on the $70 each(needing two of course) or the $130 a piece.  I will probably go with the $70 each just for money sake.<p>Sorry that I couldn't give you an answer about the performance increase or sound.  I will make a post when it gets done though.
Z||000004||Patrick||07-16-99||01:16 AM||||<br>Cooter, that was funny!  <IMG SRC="http://www.webpedia.com/animations/animations/anifiles/mailbox.gif"> <p>
Z||000005||Eric||07-16-99||06:47 PM||||Shaun, how much power do you expect to gain from the new exaust?  Is the stock exaust 2 inch pipe?  I am worried about chopping up my stock exaust because I was told it was made of stainless steel.  It doesn't look like stainless to me, but I could just be looking at the scale that developes.  In any case, I want to drive this car in the winter too and don't want the hassle of replacing the pipe after a couple of years unless the gains in power are significant.
Z||000006||batboy||07-16-99||07:44 PM||||Actually, 2 inch diameter exhaust works pretty well with V6's. I'm running 2 inch pipes on a couple of small block V8's too.  The bigger pipes will give you a couple ponies at the top end, but sometimes less torque. The cheaper and easier thing to do is to just replace the muffler and cat with free flowing ones (like Flowmaster). Headers give you the best power gain of all, but are darn expensive for a Fiero (well worth the price in my opinion though). I would think a good muffler shops can order stainless steel or aluminumized pipes and then custom bend them, if you're worried about corrosion.
Z||000007||batboy||07-16-99||07:51 PM||||I better clarify myself. My last comments about 2 inch pipes were referring to dual exhaust systems. If you are using a single muffler, then 2-1/2 pipes behind the "Y" would be better. If you are then running dual tailpipes, 2 inch ones should work fine. Maybe slap some nice big fancy exhaust tips onto the tailpipes for a better look.
Z||000008||Shaun41178||07-17-99||02:34 AM||||Eric, I expect to pic up about 5-10 hp.  This is in the upper rpm range and i do expect a loss in low rpm torque but the nitrous will make up for any loss there.  I will be using a 2.5 inch from the catback with 2.5 inch pipes coming out the muffler s into 2.5 inch tips.  All the tubing used by this muffler shop is aluminized I was told so it should last a good couple of years or longer.  I live in the salt belt so something for me to worry about.  <p>Yes the factory exhaust system from the factory is stainless steel and is 1-7/8 to 2 inches in diameter.  What you are seeing is probably scaling on the outside of the pipes but under that it is not rusting through.  I have this same scaling on mine.<p>Hopefully after this exhaust and an underdrive pulley and a few other things I hope to have over 150 hp at the wheels.  I dynoed at 130 several months ago but that was with a misfire(really robbed power above 4000 rpm) and before the ported exhaust manifolds were installed.  I am guessing I have about 140-145 hp at the wheels now without nitrous and 200-210 with nitrous<p>2.8V6 3.08 FD 3 spd auto <br>Crane HI6S ignition <br>PS-91 Coil<br>Accel 8.8 mm wires<br>Throttle Body bypass<br>Ported exhaust manifolds<br>NOS 70 hp shot<br>Future mods: Hi lift cam full port and polish of heads and intake, <br>shift kit, underdrive pulley, custom intake with K&N cone, 2.25 cat-back with flowmaster muffler<br>Currently 200 hp @ wheels before ported exhaust manifolds<br>Best e.t. to date: 14.8@91 60' 2.07 <br>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178  
